>   I was playing Nethack, under OS/2.  I started the game as "Rob" saved it 
>   after robbing a shop (teleport scroll).  I then saved the game and went 
>   back to using "nethack -u rob".  The shop keeper wandered up to me and 
>   said "Hello rob, I'm looking for Rob" and wandered off.
>
>   Has this happened to anyone else.

Sure.  NH is case sensitive when treating user names but OS/2 is not,
so rob.sav and Rob.sav really mean the same file (the newer OS/2 HPFS is
case preserving but not case sensitive).  In NH there is one exception,
though: the status line shows player's name with the first letter
capitalized, but it may still be internally different.  In addition, NH
only gets the player name information from the player at startup and uses
that name to search for a possible save file - the player name isn't stored
in the save file in any form.

